he user leaves the screen and comes back, it fires again.\n- **The slider uses `onChangeEnd`, not `onChanged`.** `onChanged` fires on every frame of a drag, which would mean dozens of events per drag with in-between amounts. `onChangeEnd` sends the amount the user actually chose.\n- **Scrolling uses `ScrollEndNotification`.** It sends one event per scroll gesture, after any fling has stopped, with the final offset. Listening to raw scroll updates would send an event every frame.\n- **`terms_accepted` only fires on tick.** The spec says \"ticked\", so unticking is not tracked. Ticking, unticking and ticking again sends the event twice.\n- **No PII.** No event includes the email or phone text. The text-field events send no properties at all.\n- **No screen-view events added.** `PosthogObserver` already tracks those, as the spec notes.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `dart format lib` was applied, and `flutter analyze` reports **No issues found**.\n- Running `flutter analyze` also ran `pub get`, which created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock` and rewrote `analysis_options.yaml`. I reverted or removed all three, so the diff only contains the two screen files.\n- I did not run the app and did not send any events to PostHog. There are no tests in the repo and I didn't add any. To check by hand, run the app against a dev PostHog project, or put a `debugPrint` in `Analytics.capture`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017aFzHVCJAu3dHBdrj14sP8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7FGgLzRoddXdqXFgSP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, sent through `Analytics.capture`. `flutter analyze` reports no issues, but I haven't run the app, sent any real events, or written tests, so I haven't seen the events fire.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`):\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** sent on the first keystroke in each field, once per visit to the screen.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** sent when the user lets go of the slider, with the final `amount`. Sending on every movement would produce dozens of events per drag.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** sent only when the box is ticked; unticking sends nothing.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** sent with `amount` and `terms` just before moving to the offers screen.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`):\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** sent once per scroll, after the list stops moving, with the final `offset`.\n\nHow often each event fires was my call, not the spec's. I aimed for one event per user action, which keeps volume down on the free tier and keeps the funnels clean. Neither the email nor the phone number is sent anywhere.\n\nRunning `flutter analyze` downloaded packages and changed some files on its own, including rewriting `analysis_options.yaml`. I reverted all of that, so the only changes are in the two screen files. To check the events by hand, run the app against a test PostHog project, or add a temporary print in `Analytics.capture`.\n\nThe full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was committed or sent to an external service."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1192,"cache_read_input_tokens":28597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1192},"output_tokens":556,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19d87fd8-f88c-4741-b856-3b7b1f9e5a56","uuid":"856ba31b-243f-47e2-876c-52da3e936bc0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:26:43.517Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7FGSDPkUVnonGU1dvd"}
